cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Kenti Macroinvertebrados"
abstract: >-
  Free desktop program for benthic macroinvertebrate data: it assigns the family of each taxon
  from its genus or species (built-in list of 5802 South American genera from GBIF, with typo
  correction) and computes the BMWP' of northwestern Argentina (Domínguez & Fernández 1998),
  completed with the Bolivian BMWP/Bol table, the ASPT' (Cammaerts et al. 2008 classes) and the
  Andean Biotic Index, plus alpha and beta diversity, PCA and an Excel report. Spanish and English interface.
type: software
